Pirates

Game code, terrain, crater lava, coconut palms, broadleaf shrubs, harbors, cargo models, upgrade models, cloth standards and synthesized
sound effects and wind/surf ambience: original work in this repository, MIT
(see the LICENSE included in the cart; source repository: ../../LICENSE).
Blender is an authoring tool; its GPL license does not change the license
of these original exported assets.

Galleon model: GalleonOGA.blend by Daniel Quevedo, CC0 / public domain.
  https://opengameart.org/content/pirate-ship-0
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Original source and source notice: art/sources/.
Modifications: tools/prepare-galleon.py normalizes orientation and scale,
assigns wood, cloth and metal materials, bakes the albedo, separates canvas
from rigid parts, adds a restrained cloth-billow morph and exports glTF.
The original source was untextured and described by its author as incomplete.

Rock0 model: reused from games/jetski, generated by
its tools/make-models.mjs; original repository art under MIT.
Shore boulders: three stones generated by tools/make-shore-rock.py
(faceted hulls with cracks, baked albedo and a flared embedded foot for
sloping terrain); original repository art under MIT.

Cannon-smoke flipbook: reused from games/arenafps, generated by
cartwheel-engine/tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs; procedural CC0 art as listed
in the engine NOTICE. Also used for the volcanic ash plume.

UI font: Cartwheel's built-in sans font; see cartwheel-engine NOTICE for
its open-font license. Engine and bundled library notices remain applicable.
